```text
FINANCE COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Finance Committee was held on Tuesday, November 4, 2025, at the Laramie
County School District #1 Boardroom and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in
attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Pete Layboum, Chairman; Ken Esquibel; Mark Moody; and Dr.
Mark Rinne.
AGENDA ITEMS
6.
APPLICATIONS’LICENSES/PERMITS:
a)
Application for a bar & grill liquor license filed with the City Clerks Office for
Redhones. LLC d./h/a HamBones Pizza, 415 XV. 17th St. Ste. 170 & 180.
Mr. Moody moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion carried with Mr. Esquibel and
Mr. Moody voting “YES’ and Dr. Rinne voting “NO.”
Kylie Soden. City Clerk, provided a staff report and Jason 1-lammer. applicant, provided additional
information.
14.
LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
a)
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and WYDOT for a Wyoming Rural
Public Transportation Grant to assist in providing local match for operating funds
for the Transit program
for Fiscal Year 2025
. (Revenue to the City)
Mr. Esqumbel moved to approve in an amount not to exceed S300.000.00. seconded by Dr. Rinne.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Erin Johnson. Transit Administrator, provided a staff report.
15.
CONSIDERATION OF BIDS/PURCHASES1REQUESTS FOR PROPOSALS:
c)
Consideration of Bid #E-3-26 for furnishing one (1) new 2025-2026 30 Ton
Articulated Dump Truck for the City of Cheyenne Landfill. (Solid Waste Fund)
Mr. Moody moved to accept the hid from Wyoming Machinery Company in an amount not to
exceed $501,541.25, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion carried by unanimous voice votc.
Sam Quattrinm, Landfill Manager, provided a staff report and TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager.
provided additional information. Committee members Esquibel and Moody commented on the
item.
```

