e)
Consideration of Bid #E-5-26 for furnishing one (1) new Backhoe Loader for the
City of Cheyenne Cemetery. (2021 Specific Purpose Option Tax Fund)
Mr. Moody moved to accept the bid from Wyoming Machinery Company in an amount not to
exceed S 174,437.50, seconded by Mr. Esquibel. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Jason Sanchez, Community Recreation & Events Director, provided a staff report.
U
Consideration of Bid #E-6-26 for furnishing ten (10) new Four-Door 2025/2026
Model Utility Police Interceptors. (2023-2026 Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
Mr. Moody moved to accept the bid from Duval Ford in an amount not to exceed $662,550.00,
seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Lieutenant Neil Durante, Police Department, provided a staff report and committee members
Esquihel, Moody, and Rinne commented on the item.
g)
Consideration of Bid #E-7-26 for furnishing one (1) new 2025-2026 3/4 Ton, Crew
Cab, Full Size Pickup Truck, 4 X 4 with a 6.75 FT Box. (2023-2026 Optional 1%
Sales Tax Fund and General Fund)
Mr. Esquibcl moved to accept the bid from Fremont Motor Company in an amount not to exceed
$102,083.00, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Battalion Chief Ryan Anderson, Fire Rescue Department, provided a staff report and committee
member Moody commented on the item.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Public Services Committee, the
